// The same two pins, and one character different: `? Button` makes the
// assignment CONDITIONAL.
//
//      Led = Button        assigns every cycle -- Led follows
//      Led = 1 ? Button    assigns WHEN Button is true -- Led latches
//
// When the guard is false the rule does nothing at all, so Led keeps whatever
// it had. Press Button and let go: the lamp stays lit. That is not a bug, it
// is what `?` means, and it is the first thing about candyspeak that catches
// people out. Watch it on the trace: Button returns to zero, Led does not.
//
// To turn it off you have to say so:
//
//      Led = 0 ? !Button

#digital Button in pullup 2
#digital Led    out       13

Led = 1 ? Button
